.TH INVF-IMPORT 8 "2026-09" "InvariantFS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
invf\-import \- bulk tree importer for InvariantFS volumes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B invf\-import
.I volume
.I src\-dir
.RI [ exclude\-dir\-name ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B invf\-import
recursively imports a host directory tree into an unmounted InvariantFS
volume at the engine level (no FUSE mount required). It creates
directories, regular files, symlinks, and special nodes (FIFO, socket,
character, block) with full format\-v2 metadata (type, mode, uid/gid,
mtime/atime).
.PP
Optional trailing arguments name directories to exclude from the walk
(e.g.
.BR \.git " " node_modules ).
Maximum recursion depth is 32.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INVFS_IMPORT_PREFIX
If set, imports under an existing volume subdirectory instead of the root.
The target directory must already exist.
.TP
.B INVFS_IMPORT_KEEP_OWNER
If set to 1, preserves the source file\(aqs uid/gid. The default (0) creates
all files as root (uid=0, gid=0).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success (skipped entries are non\-fatal); 1 on open or
bad\-superblock errors; 2 on usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR invf\-mkfs (8),
.BR invf\-sweep (8),
.BR invarifs (7)
